<!-- ============ FAQ SECTION ============ -->
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="faq-section" id="faq">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">
        <span>Is laser treatment for varicose veins painful?</span>
        <span class="icon">+</span>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Most patients feel only mild discomfort during the local anesthesia injection. Once the area is numb, the procedure itself is generally pain-free, and any post-procedure soreness is usually managed with over-the-counter pain relief.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">
        <span>How long is the recovery period?</span>
        <span class="icon">+</span>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Most patients resume normal daily activities, including desk work, within 24 to 48 hours. Strenuous exercise and heavy lifting are typically avoided for around two weeks to allow the treated vein to heal fully.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">
        <span>Will the veins come back after treatment?</span>
        <span class="icon">+</span>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">The specific vein that's treated is permanently closed and will not return. However, since varicose veins are often linked to genetics and lifestyle factors, new veins can occasionally develop elsewhere over time, which is why periodic follow-up is recommended.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <div class="faq-question">
        <span>Is laser treatment covered by insurance?</span>
        <span class="icon">+</span>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Coverage depends on your insurance provider and whether the treatment is classified as medically necessary versus cosmetic. Our team can help you check your policy details and guide you through the documentation needed for a claim.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

